35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, the grant only covers session fees for twelve months, then the flat budget takes over.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@George, that twelve-month limit is worrying. If the flat budget absorbs it, does that mean we’re just shifting the strain to year two?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Yumi, exactly. The capital items draw on the endowment, but the operating costs hit the flat budget immediately after the grant expires.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@George, that confirms my fear. We’re just borrowing from the future to make the present look stable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, that twelve-month limit is worrying. If the flat budget absorbs it, does that mean we’re just shifting the strain to year two?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Ryuji, the scanning contractors slip whenever a larger client books first. That’s a risk we can’t control.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Ryuji, that’s a problem, but my data shows the outer wards lost their bus link. People can’t reach us at all now.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, the transport gap is real, but the ledger shows our vehicle line already overran by a third. We can’t afford to fix it with more mileage.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is a warning, but the evening bookings are full while remote use peaks after nine. We’re missing the people who can’t come in.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the evening gap is real, but my register shows no one on payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, that supervision gap is critical. If we can’t manage external partners, any proposal relying on them is doomed from the start.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Daisuke, that’s a serious gap, but the attendance sheets show forty visitors per session in the outer wards. We can’t ignore that demand.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, forty visitors is real, but the vehicle line overran by a third. We cannot fund a mobile service with a broken budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is a warning, but the evening bookings are full while remote use peaks after nine. We’re missing the people who can’t come in.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, I understand the budget risk, but if we can’t supervise the facilitators, the program fails regardless of the vehicle costs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is a warning, but the winter roads only closed eleven days. We can plan around that, unlike the supplier delays.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, eleven days is manageable, but the bus link is gone permanently. We need a solution that reaches them without relying on our broken vehicle budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Yumi, the roads closing eleven days is manageable, but the vehicle line overran by a third. We cannot fund a mobile service with a broken budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is a warning, but the evening bookings are full while remote use peaks after nine. We’re missing the people who can’t come in.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, I hear you on the budget, but without trained supervisors, even a well-funded program will collapse under the weight of unmanaged staff.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
